TEXT 128 704 Left 1 ;HOW TO VIEW WAVEFORMS  (note only - you may delete it, the circuit is not affected)\n1. Click Run (running-man icon). A black waveform window opens; it is empty at first.\n2. In this schematic, put the mouse on a wire marked VIEW. The cursor becomes a red probe. Click.\n3. That voltage is drawn in the waveform window, with its name, e.g. V(out), in the same colour above it.\n4. Click the other VIEW wires to add more signals. All share one time axis (read left to right).\n5. One signal per pane: click the waveform window, Plot Settings > Add Plot Pane, click the new pane, then click the next wire.\n6. Remove a trace: Plot Settings > Delete Traces, then click the trace name. Press Esc to stop deleting.\nSignals:  INPUT Vin = V(n002) (wire from V1)   |   OUTPUT = V(vout)
